@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "osb.integration"

Feature: OSB DXP Cloud Subscription
	Testing automatic subscriptions to DXP Cloud for customers on OSB accounts with DXP cloud subscriptions.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | dxpcloud.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | DXPCloud                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                                |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | dxpcloud.customer2                       |
	| Email Address | dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | DXPCloud                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer2                                |
	* I create a support user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | dxpcloud.user1                       |
	| Email Address | dxpcloud.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | DXPCloud                             |
	| Last Name     | User1                                |
	* I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code   | DXCZENDXCZEN                  | |
	| Name   | Dxczen - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Region | United States                 | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	| Tier   | T1                            | |
	* I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code   | DXCDUPDXCDUP                  | |
	| Name   | Dxcdup - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Region | United States                 | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	| Tier   | T1                            | |
	* I assign the contact with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Developer |
	* I assign the contact with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Watcher |
	* I generate static start and end dates
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Cloud Subscription HA Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Limited Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Limited Subscription"
	* I wait for "1" minutes
	* the support organization with the code "DXCZENDXCZEN" should be part of the support site

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Dxcdup - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Dxczen - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Dxcdup - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| DXCZENDXCZEN |
	| DXCDUPDXCDUP |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Limited Subscription"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| DXCZENDXCZEN |
	| DXCDUPDXCDUP |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| dxpcloud.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken     |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| New Subscription(s) for Dxczen - ${staticProjectName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Dxcdup - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Dxczen - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Dxcdup - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I log out and log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I tear down the following user email addresses from the DXP Cloud subscription list
	| dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| dxpcloud.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken     |

Scenario: View subscription
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	@ help.center.smoke = "true"
	Users on accounts with DXP cloud subscriptions should be subscribed to DXP cloud

	Given the user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed on DXP cloud
	And the user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed on DXP cloud

Scenario: View subscription after removal from one account
	Users removed from one account with DXP cloud subscriptions while remaining on another should be subscribed to DXP cloud

	Given I assign the contact with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Dxcdup - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Developer |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Dxcdup - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Watcher |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Dxcdup - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Cloud Subscription HA Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Dxcdup - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Limited Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Limited Subscription"
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the support organization with the code "DXCDUPDXCDUP" should be part of the support site
	When I remove customer contacts with the following email addresses from the account "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}"
	| dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I remove customer contacts with the following email addresses from the account "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}"
	| dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed on DXP cloud
	And the user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed on DXP cloud

Scenario: View no subscription after offering expiration
	Users on accounts with expired DXP cloud subscriptions should not be subscribed to DXP cloud

	Given I generate past static start and end dates
	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "DXP Cloud Subscription HA Production" to have the following values
	| End Date          | ${staticPastEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date | ${staticPastOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual         | false                        | |
	| Start Date        | ${staticPastStartDate}       | |
	| Status            | Approved                     | |
	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Limited Subscription" to have the following values
	| End Date          | ${staticPastEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date | ${staticPastOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual         | false                        | |
	| Start Date        | ${staticPastStartDate}       | |
	| Status            | Approved                     | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Limited Subscription"
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed on DXP cloud
	And the user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed on DXP cloud

Scenario: View no subscription after offering cancellation
	Users on accounts with cancelled DXP cloud subscriptions should not be subscribed to DXP cloud

	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "DXP Cloud Subscription HA Production" to have the following values
	| End Date          | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual         | false                    | |
	| Start Date        | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status            | Cancelled                | |
	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Limited Subscription" to have the following values
	| End Date          | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual         | false                    | |
	| Start Date        | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status            | Cancelled                | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Limited Subscription"
	And I remove customer contacts with the following email addresses from the account "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}"
	| dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I remove customer contacts with the following email addresses from the account "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}"
	| dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed on DXP cloud
	And the user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed on DXP cloud

Scenario: View no subscription after offering removal
	Users on accounts with removed DXP cloud subscriptions should not be subscribed to DXP cloud

	Given I generate past static start and end dates
	And I delete a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "DXP Cloud Subscription HA Production"
	And I delete a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Limited Subscription"
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed on DXP cloud
	And the user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed on DXP cloud

Scenario: View no subscription after customer removal
	Users that are no longer on a DXP cloud accounts should not be subscribed to DXP cloud

	Given I remove customer contacts with the following email addresses from the account "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}"
	| dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed on DXP cloud
	And the user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed on DXP cloud 
	When I remove customer contacts with the following email addresses from the account "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}"
	| dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed on DXP cloud
	And the user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed on DXP cloud

Scenario: Request passport access
	Users on accounts with DXP cloud subscriptions should be able to request passports from the passport page

	Given I update the support password for user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I go to the Liferay University Passport Access page
	Then I should be able to the view the Liferay University Passport Access text for users with full access to the form
	And I request passport access with the following values
	| End User First Name    | DXPCloud                                 |
	| End User Last Name     | Customer1                                |
	| Company Name           | Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}            |
	| End User Email Address | dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	When I log out and log into the support homepage as "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I go to the Liferay University Passport Access page
	Then I should be able to the view the Liferay University Passport Access text for users with full access to the form
	And I request passport access with the following values
	| End User First Name    | DXPCloud                                 |
	| End User Last Name     | Customer2                                |
	| Company Name           | Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}            |
	| End User Email Address | dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |

Scenario: Request passport access as user with dxp cloud customer email
	Users with similar email addresses to other users on accounts with DXP cloud subscriptions should be able to request passports from the passport page

	Given I update the support password for user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "dxpcloud.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dxpcloud.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dxpcloud.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Guest"
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "dxpcloud.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I go to the Liferay University Passport Access page
	Then I should be able to the view the Liferay University Passport Access text for users with full access to the form
	And I request passport access with the following values
	| End User First Name    | DXPCloud                             |
	| End User Last Name     | User1                                |
	| Company Name           | Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}        |
	| End User Email Address | dxpcloud.user1@lrcustomer.com.broken |

Scenario: View downloads page
	Users on accounts with DXP cloud subscriptions should be able to view the downloads page

	Given I update the support password for user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I go to the Downloads page
	And I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.2" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.2 Fix Pack 2" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.2 Fix Pack 1" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.1" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.1 Fix Pack 14" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.1 Fix Pack 13" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.0" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.0 Fix Pack 86" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.0 Fix Pack 85" should be visible
	When I log out and log into the support homepage as "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I go to the Downloads page
	And I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.2" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.2 Fix Pack 2" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.2 Fix Pack 1" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.1" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.1 Fix Pack 14" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.1 Fix Pack 13" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.0" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.0 Fix Pack 86" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.0 Fix Pack 85" should be visible

Scenario: View self provisioning page
	Users on accounts with DXP cloud subscriptions should be able to view the self provisioning page

	Given I update the support password for user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I go to the Self Provisioning page
	Then I should be able to view the following options in the Self Provisioning portlet
	| Project | Dxczen - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product | DXP                           |
	| Version | 7.2                           |
	| Version | 7.1                           |
	| Version | 7.0                           |
	When I log out and log into the support homepage as "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I go to the Self Provisioning page
	Then I should be able to view the following options in the Self Provisioning portlet
	| Project | Dxczen - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product | DXP                           |
	| Version | 7.2                           |
	| Version | 7.1                           |
	| Version | 7.0                           |

Scenario: Download self provisioning license
	Users on accounts with DXP cloud subscriptions should be able to download the self provisioning page

	Given I update the support password for user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "${staticSupportUserTestPassword}"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
