Scenario: View subscription after removal and reassignment to account
	Users that are removed from and reassigned to a DXP cloud account should be subscribed to DXP cloud

	Given I remove customer contacts with the following email addresses from the account "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}"
	| dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed on DXP cloud
	And the user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed on DXP cloud 
	When I remove customer contacts with the following email addresses from the account "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}"
	| dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed on DXP cloud
	And the user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed on DXP cloud
	When I assign the contact with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Developer |
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed on DXP cloud
	And the user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed on DXP cloud
	When I assign the contact with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Watcher |
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed on DXP cloud
	And the user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed on DXP cloud